[SIZE=6][B][COLOR=#FF0368]BiteDisplays[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[I]NPCs, holograms, and item and block displays, placed and styled in-game.[/I]

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#FF0368]▸ Overview[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
Your spawn deserves more than signs. BiteDisplays lets you place NPCs with real player skins, floating text, and displays of any item or block right where you stand. Style them with gradients and hex colors, have them run commands when players click them, and manage all of it in-game with one simple command.

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#FF0368]▸ Key Features[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B][COLOR=#4ECDC4]Four Entity Types:[/COLOR][/B] NPCs with skins and equipment, multi-line text displays, and item and block displays.
[*][B][COLOR=#4ECDC4]Click Actions:[/COLOR][/B] NPCs and item and block displays run a command when right-clicked, with {player} filled in. NPCs can play a sound too.
[*][B][COLOR=#4ECDC4]Modern Formatting:[/COLOR][/B] MiniMessage gradients, HEX colors, and decorations in every name and line.
[*][B][COLOR=#4ECDC4]Point & Edit:[/COLOR][/B] New entities are selected for you. Look at any other one to select it, then move, inspect, or remove it.
[*][B][COLOR=#4ECDC4]Spigot, Paper & Purpur:[/COLOR][/B] One jar that runs on all three, tested on each.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#FF0368]▸ Formatting[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
Names, descriptions, and text lines all understand MiniMessage.

[LIST]
[*][B]<red>Ruby[/B] / [B]<gold>Gilded[/B] - Named colors.
[*][B]<#FF0368>Magenta[/B] - HEX colors.
[*][B]<gradient:#FF0368:#4ECDC4>Bitesize</gradient>[/B] - Smooth gradients (rainbows too).
[*][B]<bold>[/B], [B]<italic>[/B], [B]<underlined>[/B], [B]<strikethrough>[/B] - Decorations.
[/LIST]

On Paper and Purpur, text keeps every MiniMessage feature, like custom fonts.

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#FF0368]▸ Additional Features[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]Every single message is completely configurable in the messages.yml.
[*]Smart TAB completion suggests actions, glow colors, every game sound, online players for skins, and the lines on your selected text display.
[*]An equipment menu to dress your NPCs in any armor and held items.
[*]Bouncing item displays, glowing in any color, and text that turns to face players.
[*]Turn NPCs, item, block, or text displays on or off individually.
[*]Lightweight: entities are vanilla mannequins and displays, saved to one file and respawned as their chunks load.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#FF0368]▸ NPC Commands[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B][COLOR=#4ECDC4]/bd npc create <name>[/COLOR][/B] - Create an NPC where you stand
[*][B][COLOR=#4ECDC4]/bd npc skin <player>[/COLOR][/B] - Use a player's skin
[*][B][COLOR=#4ECDC4]/bd npc name [name][/COLOR][/B] - Set the name
[*][B][COLOR=#4ECDC4]/bd npc desc [text][/COLOR][/B] - Set the line under the name
[*][B][COLOR=#4ECDC4]/bd npc glow [color][/COLOR][/B] - Glow in a color
[*][B][COLOR=#4ECDC4]/bd npc cmd [command][/COLOR][/B] - Run a command on right-click
[*][B][COLOR=#4ECDC4]/bd npc sound [sound][/COLOR][/B] - Play a sound on right-click
[*][B][COLOR=#4ECDC4]/bd npc equipment[/COLOR][/B] - Open the equipment menu
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#FF0368]▸ Text Display Commands[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B][COLOR=#4ECDC4]/bd text create [text][/COLOR][/B] - Create a text display where you stand
[*][B][COLOR=#4ECDC4]/bd text addline <text>[/COLOR][/B] - Add a line
[*][B][COLOR=#4ECDC4]/bd text editline <line> <text>[/COLOR][/B] - Replace a line
[*][B][COLOR=#4ECDC4]/bd text delline <line>[/COLOR][/B] - Remove a line
[*][B][COLOR=#4ECDC4]/bd text background <hex>[/COLOR][/B] - Set the background color
[*][B][COLOR=#4ECDC4]/bd text glow [color][/COLOR][/B] - Glow in a color name or HEX color
[*][B][COLOR=#4ECDC4]/bd text billboard <true|false>[/COLOR][/B] - Turn to face players
[*][B][COLOR=#4ECDC4]/bd text size <scale>[/COLOR][/B] - Scale the text
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#FF0368]▸ Item & Block Display Commands[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B][COLOR=#4ECDC4]/bd item create[/COLOR][/B] / [B][COLOR=#4ECDC4]/bd block create[/COLOR][/B] - Display the item or block you're holding
[*][B][COLOR=#4ECDC4]/bd <item|block> rotate <yaw|pitch> <degrees>[/COLOR][/B] - Rotate it
[*][B][COLOR=#4ECDC4]/bd <item|block> size <scale>[/COLOR][/B] - Scale it
[*][B][COLOR=#4ECDC4]/bd <item|block> name [name][/COLOR][/B] - Show a name above it
[*][B][COLOR=#4ECDC4]/bd <item|block> cmd [command][/COLOR][/B] - Run a command on right-click
[*][B][COLOR=#4ECDC4]/bd <item|block> glowing <true|false>[/COLOR][/B] - Make it glow
[*][B][COLOR=#4ECDC4]/bd item bouncing <true|false>[/COLOR][/B] - Bob the item up and down
[/LIST]

Leave out a [value] to remove it.

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#FF0368]▸ Managing Entities & Permissions[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B][COLOR=#4ECDC4]/bd select[/COLOR][/B] - Select the entity you're looking at [I](bitedisplays.manage)[/I]
[*][B][COLOR=#4ECDC4]/bd movehere[/COLOR][/B] - Move your selection to you [I](bitedisplays.manage)[/I]
[*][B][COLOR=#4ECDC4]/bd remove[/COLOR][/B] - Remove your selection [I](bitedisplays.manage)[/I]
[*][B][COLOR=#4ECDC4]/bd info[/COLOR][/B] - Show your selection's details [I](bitedisplays.manage)[/I]
[*][B][COLOR=#4ECDC4]/bd list [type][/COLOR][/B] - List every entity, or one type [I](bitedisplays.manage)[/I]
[*][B][COLOR=#4ECDC4]/bd save[/COLOR][/B] / [B][COLOR=#4ECDC4]/bd reload[/COLOR][/B] - Save entities / reload config & messages [I](bitedisplays.admin)[/I]
[*][B]bitedisplays.npc, .text, .item, .block[/B] - Each entity type's commands.
[*][B]bitedisplays.*[/B] - Every BiteDisplays permission.
[/LIST]

All permissions default to op. [I]Every command also works as /bitedisplays.[/I]

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#FF0368]▸ Configuration[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B][COLOR=#4ECDC4]Features:[/COLOR][/B] Toggle NPCs, item, block, and text displays individually.
[*][B][COLOR=#4ECDC4]Selection:[/COLOR][/B] How far away /bd select reaches.
[*][B][COLOR=#4ECDC4]Text:[/COLOR][/B] The default first line and background of new text displays.
[*][B][COLOR=#4ECDC4]Animations:[/COLOR][/B] The height, speed, and smoothness of bouncing items.
[/LIST]

[SPOILER=config.yml]
[CODE]features:
  npc: true
  item: true     # item displays
  block: true    # block displays
  text: true     # text displays

selection:
  range: 5.0

text:
  default-line: "Text Display"
  default-background: "#64000000"

animations:
  bounce:
    interval: 4
    height: 0.12
    speed: 0.15[/CODE]
[/SPOILER]

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#FF0368]▸ Messages[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
Every message lives in messages.yml, grouped into errors, messages, help, info, and gui, with full MiniMessage support. Set your own prefix and error prefix, rename the entity types, and use variables like <type>, <id>, <name>, <command>, and <line>.
New messages added in updates are filled in automatically, so you never have to regenerate the file.

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#FF0368]▸ Compatibility[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]Minecraft:[/B] 26.3
[*][B]Servers:[/B] Spigot, Paper, and Purpur
[*][B]Java:[/B] 25
[/LIST]
[I]On first start, the server downloads the Kotlin standard library once, so it needs internet access.[/I]

